{"issue": true, "summary": "The `catch` block on line 44 is empty and silently swallows all promise rejections, which can hide runtime errors and prevent proper error handling in asynchronous function calls.", "edits": [{"path": "index.js", "old": "		try {
			await result;
		} catch {}

		// Decrement active count and process next queued function
		next();", "new": "		try {
			await result;
		} catch (error) {
			next();
			throw error;
		}

		// Decrement active count and process next queued function
		next();"}]}
